More ideas for hack:
Vial: allows you to dip in the sink and get more potions, or a vial of 
radio active  waste.

Cloak of pockets. Works like a bag of holding but it has a limited number 
of slots and you can only apply it if it is being worn. A cursed one would 
randomly move stuff around while  lying to you about what pocket something 
is in,  and a blessed one would occasionly tell you if an item was cursed or 
blessed.

Figurine of Clonning: If you are at low levels of hit points when you use 
this the clone replaces you, leaving you at full health, but you droped 
all your possetions. Cursed, you will be possesed and lose control of the 
character temporaly. Blessed you gain more hit points. If you use it when 
you are not at low hit points, you gain a follower of the same race, who 
looks like you and has almost the same stats. If the figurine is blessed, 
it may almost be as powerfull as you are. If cursed, it will attack you.

This one has to do with my last post on new classes. 
Telephone booth: this is like a sink or a fountan, except when you enter a 
telephone both into a one by one room. Inside you can.
Take off all your clothes and have a percent chance of changing into a 
super-hero when you put them back on (ie. gaining some new intrinsics or 
increasing your abilities. These intrinsics may be things that you can't 
get any other way except by items or by  being a certain class). If this 
is the case you get a message like: "You knew there was something strange 
about the grid bug that bit you on level <give a number>, it was glowing." 
" You are no longer just a mere <class name>, you have become a super-hero."
"You must chose a new name to protect your friends and family, and to 
strike fear into the hearts of those cowardly superstious monsters. 
Chose a new heroic name:" 
If you hit return without typing anything in you get: "You are a brave 
<man/woman> to face the dangers of being a hero without a secret identity."
Other  wise is says "<the name you typed in>" and a joke about the name.
If you chose a heroic ID shopkeepers will recognize you and ask for 
autographs, but the will raise the price because they think you can afford 
it. You may change to a secret ID removing your armor in a phone booth. 
But you will not be able to use any intrinsics while in your secret ID. If 
you have no ID you won't be able to change. So this problem will occur all 
the time, but on the other hand you will have the intrinsics no matter 
what you are wearing. A secret ID hero will be asked what his symbol is 
and his armor will be marked with that symbol. Once the character gets a 
unique attribue like the identification ablity of the priest, leaping 
ability without boots, or a  built in spell (newve fails can't be over used),
the character will not be able to get new intrinsics from a phone booth.
The chance of this happening is slight, but it increases per-level, (at 
high levels you are almost a super-hero anyway unless you had real bad 
luck.) Some bad things might happen if you do this, but I'm not sure what. 
I'm dropping the super-hero as a class idea.

